    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Track object matting from a seed mask or a target description.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Target video segment id (raw id, no seg_id= prefix)\r\n          --segment-time TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Time offset from the target segment visible start, in seconds by\r\n                              default; supports s/ms/us suffix\r\n          --seed-mask-rle-json, --mask-rle-json TEXT \r\n                              Seed mask RLE JSON object or @path, e.g.\r\n                              {\"counts\":[...],\"size\":[height,width]}\r\n          --target-object-desc, --sam3-target-object-desc TEXT \r\n                              Target object description for seed mask generation; mutually\r\n                              exclusive with --seed-mask-rle-json\r\n          --feather TEXT      Matting feather, default 0\r\n          --expansion, --expand, --edge-size TEXT \r\n                              Matting edge expansion / edge size, default 0\r\n          --reverse           Reverse the final matting result\r\n          --sam3-debug-artifacts \r\n                              Keep the extracted seed frame and write SAM3 request/response\r\n                              debug JSON files when using --target-object-desc\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Track object matting from an externally supplied seed mask\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo object-matting-track --ref local://demo --seg-id <UUID> \\\r\n      --segment-time 0 --seed-mask-rle-json '{\"counts\":[2,2],\"size\":[2,2]}' \\\r\n      --feather 0 --edge-size 0\r\n  # Or describe the target object and let lyra-cli generate the seed mask\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo object-matting-track --ref local://demo --seg-id <UUID> \\\r\n      --segment-time 0 --target-object-desc \"phone\" --feather 0 --edge-size 0\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - --seed-mask-rle-json and --target-object-desc are mutually exclusive. --mask-rle-json is accepted as a compatibility alias.\r\n  - With --target-object-desc, lyra-cli extracts the seed frame, uploads it, requests SAM3, then feeds the returned RLE into the existing seed mask path.\r\n  - Use --sam3-debug-artifacts to keep the extracted seed frame and write sam3_request.json / sam3_response.json.\r\n  - lyra-cli converts the RLE mask to seed mask content; videoeditor maps segment relative time to source time and runs mask tracking.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Track object matting from a seed mask or a target description.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Target video segment id (raw id, no seg_id= prefix)\r\n          --segment-time TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Time offset from the target segment visible start, in seconds by\r\n                              default; supports s/ms/us suffix\r\n          --seed-mask-rle-json, --mask-rle-json TEXT \r\n                              Seed mask RLE JSON object or @path, e.g.\r\n                              {\"counts\":[...],\"size\":[height,width]}\r\n          --target-object-desc, --sam3-target-object-desc TEXT \r\n                              Target object description for seed mask generation; mutually\r\n                              exclusive with --seed-mask-rle-json\r\n          --feather TEXT      Matting feather, default 0\r\n          --expansion, --expand, --edge-size TEXT \r\n                              Matting edge expansion / edge size, default 0\r\n          --reverse           Reverse the final matting result\r\n          --sam3-debug-artifacts \r\n                              Keep the extracted seed frame and write SAM3 request/response\r\n                              debug JSON files when using --target-object-desc\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Track object matting from an externally supplied seed mask\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo object-matting-track --ref local://demo --seg-id <UUID> \\\r\n      --segment-time 0 --seed-mask-rle-json '{\"counts\":[2,2],\"size\":[2,2]}' \\\r\n      --feather 0 --edge-size 0\r\n  # Or describe the target object and let lyra-cli generate the seed mask\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo object-matting-track --ref local://demo --seg-id <UUID> \\\r\n      --segment-time 0 --target-object-desc \"phone\" --feather 0 --edge-size 0\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - --seed-mask-rle-json and --target-object-desc are mutually exclusive. --mask-rle-json is accepted as a compatibility alias.\r\n  - With --target-object-desc, lyra-cli extracts the seed frame, uploads it, requests SAM3, then feeds the returned RLE into the existing seed mask path.\r\n  - Use --sam3-debug-artifacts to keep the extracted seed frame and write sam3_request.json / sam3_response.json.\r\n  - lyra-cli converts the RLE mask to seed mask content; videoeditor maps segment relative time to source time and runs mask tracking.\r\n",
